Z||000000||SLYGUY||09-25-2001||04:11 AM||||I had a problem with my 88GT idling rough. The check engine light came on also. I ran a diagnostic and it flashed the code for the EGR. <BR>I took a look. The EGR looked to  be original so I replaced it. Idle was a little better. <BR>The EGR was a universal and I was told to use a #11 orifice washer on it. This reduces the flow somewhat but that is the one that Kragen auto parts said to use. (Checker Auto in some states)<P>The plastic tube leading away from the EGR is discoloring and melting a little. Check engine light came on again. Is this a sign of a bad NEW EGR?<P>This replacement has the vacuum fitting on the other side facing the left taillight. The original faced 180 degrees the opposite direction. <BR>Is there a kink or something? Are hot exhaust gases supposed to travel up that little plastic hose?<P>Thanks again for your help<P>Sly||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fiero_Freak||09-25-2001||07:47 AM||||   I had the same alignment of the vacuum input.  I had to put a wrench on it to turn it around.  As far as the tube goes, I guess it's possible for it to be leaking that way but it's kinda doubtful.  I would be willing to bet that your tube from the egr bracket to the intake it clogged.  Just pop off the top of the intake and unclog the lower oriface where the egr tube plugs in.  I've had 3 v-6's and ALL had that port plugged.  GM put the tube at the lowest point of the intake where all the oil from the pvc tube would collect.  This way the exhaust gases could burn it into a brick!  Good luck. <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg"> <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||09-25-2001||12:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>Are hot exhaust gases supposed to travel up that little plastic hose?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>No.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||09-25-2001||01:36 PM||||It's best to just get an ACdelco EGR valve.  Fiero Store sells them or get them from a GM dealer.  They are facing the correct direction and just bolt right on... none of that universal crap.  When my EGR valve died, the light only came on when driving over 50mph.  I believe the Fiero Store sells the EGR tube also.||||reg||1
